From 28cf60c91cc1cee6c71af82a6acc45225e78cc84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:54:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/49] R2: pack handlers that use the backend run after Load
 has returned; decode errors inside Load are not retried; a Load without data
 fails closed

repack (prune, copy) and repair packs save or upload blobs from the blob
handler. The coalesced pack stream called the handler inside the backend
Load callback, while the pack read held a connection: with one backend
connection repair packs deadlocked. These callers now use
loadBlobsFromPackReleased: one request per window, the connection is
released before a blob is decoded or handed over. Restore keeps the
coalesced path (its handler makes no backend call).

In the coalesced path an error of the decoder in a completely read window
(for example an index entry with an invalid length) cancels the request and
is returned once, instead of being replayed by the retry backend until its
budget ends and the circuit breaker opens. A Load that returns nil without
taking the range to its end no longer returns success with nothing
delivered: the open blobs are decoded from zero bytes, as stock does, so each
fails authentication and is recovered from another copy or reported.

No hash or MAC check is changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
